<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal debt/GDP ratio to fall to 68 pct 1997.</title>
<headline>Portugal debt/GDP ratio to fall to 68 pct 1997.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's ratio of public debt to Gross Domestic Product (GDP) is expected to fall to 68 percent in 1997 from 70.7 percent in 1996, Finance Minister Antonio Sousa Franco told a news conference.  </p>
<p>&quot;The ratio of public debt (to GDP) in 1997 will be 68 percent,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The news conference was called to give details of the government's 1997 budget proposals presented to parliament.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
